1
00:04:16,666 --> 00:04:22,666
His name is Deth. He hunts Trancers. Even in the 20th Century.

2
00:08:33,333 --> 00:08:39,333
Trancers is a science fiction, crime film directed by Charles Band.

3
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:56,000
Angel City trooper Jack Deth is sent back in time from 2247 to 1985 L.A.

4
00:17:06,666 --> 00:17:12,666
to inhabit the body of his ancestor.

5
00:21:23,333 --> 00:21:29,333
Deth's assignment is to find his archenemy, Whistler, who turns people into zombies, before
the fiend is able to kill all the ancestors of the future's governing council.

6
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:46,000
Trooper Jack Deth, played by Tim Thomerson.

7
00:29:56,666 --> 00:30:02,666
Leena, played by Helen Hunt.

8
00:34:13,333 --> 00:34:19,333
Hap Ashby, played by Biff Manard.

9
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:36,000
Martin Whistler / Detective Weisling, played by Michael Stefani.

10
00:42:46,666 --> 00:42:52,666
McNulty, played by Art LaFleur.

11
00:47:03,333 --> 00:47:09,333
Ruth Raines, played by Telma Hopkins.

12
00:51:20,000 --> 00:51:26,000
Trancers (also released as Future Cop) is a 1984 American science fiction action film
directed by Charles Band and starring Tim Thomerson, Helen Hunt, and Art LaFleur.

13
00:55:36,666 --> 00:55:42,666
It is the first film in the Trancers series.

14
00:59:53,333 --> 00:59:59,333
Thomerson plays Jack Deth, a Philip Marlowe-esque police detective from the 23rd
century who travels to the 1980s to bring his old nemesis to justice.

15
01:04:10,000 --> 01:04:16,000
The film portrays a unique method of time travel: people can travel back in time by injecting
themselves with a drug that allows them to take over the body of an ancestor.

16
01:08:26,666 --> 01:08:32,666
The film explores themes of rescue, police, fight, detective, santa claus.

17
01:12:43,333 --> 01:12:49,333
The tone is thought_provoking.
